      "id": 1,
      "text": "Alcolu was established between 1885 and 1890 by D.W. Alderman as a company mill town for his timber business.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcolu%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Alcolu comes from the first letters of Alderman, his friend Algernon Coldwell, and Alderman's daughter, Lula.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcolu%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Company employees in Alcolu were once paid in metal coins called babbits, which could only be used at the company store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcolu%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The company store in Alcolu was one of the first department stores in South Carolina and featured the town's first elevator.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcolu%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "D.W. Alderman founded the Alcolu and Paroda railroads and built the Alcolu railroad depot to support the local lumber industry.",
